      {
        "finding_id": "section-9e22d39b174b4fc82d1a",
        "file": "ournavybarbaryco00alle_ournavybarbaryco00alle_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Our navy and the Barbary corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/ournavybarbaryco00alle",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Allen, Gardner Weld, 1856-1944"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1905-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e15e3a557e79edec2ea71b2b5ccd1015a5ec882a666c35aba27115b05eadb074",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Franklin,  while  minister  to  France,  received  a  letter \nfrom  a  certain  M.  Salva  dated  Algiers,  April  1, 1783, \nwhich  related  the  narrow  escape  of  two  American  ves- \nsels which  had  recently  sailed  from  Marseilles,  adding : \n*'  Some  secret  enemies,  whom  I  know,  having  given \ninformation  to  this  Regency  of  their  departure,  nine \narmed  ships  immediately  sailed  to  wait  for  them  at \nCape  Palos.  It  is  to  be  presumed  that  the  Americans \nhad  passed  the  Straits.\"  Franklin  wrote  to  R.  R.  Liv- \ningston, Secretary  of  Foreign  Affairs,  on  the  subject, \nJuly  25,  1783,  as  follows  :  \"  You  will  see  by  the  en- \nclosed copy  of  a  letter  I  received  from  Algiers,  the \ndanger  two  of  our  ships  escaped  last  winter.  I  think \nit  not  improbable  that  those  rovers  may  be  privately \nencouraged  by  the  English  to  fall  upon  us  and  to  pre- \nvent our  interfering  in  the  carrying  trade  ;  for  I  have \nin  London  heard  it  is  a  maxim  among  the  merchants, \nthat  if  there  were  no  Algiers^  it  would  he  worth  Eng- \nland's while  to  build  one.  I  wonder,  however,  that  the \nrest  of  Europe  do  not  combine  to  destroy  those  nests \nand  secure  commerce  from  their  future  piracies.\"  ^",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1783
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
