      {
        "finding_id": "section-70d4501fa6e0a6d3f0a2",
        "file": "ournavybarbaryco00alle_ournavybarbaryco00alle_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Our navy and the Barbary corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/ournavybarbaryco00alle",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Allen, Gardner Weld, 1856-1944"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1905-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e15e3a557e79edec2ea71b2b5ccd1015a5ec882a666c35aba27115b05eadb074",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Meanwhile  efforts  at  making  peace  with  Algiers \nwere  not  abandoned.  The  number  of  captives  had \nnow  been  increased  to  a  hundred  and  nineteen,  and \ntheir  redemption  had  become  correspondingly  difficult \nand  expensive.  The  Swedish  consul,  Matthias  Skjolde- \nbrand,  and  his  brother  were  much  interested  in  the \nfate  of  the  Americans.  The  consul,  on  account  of  his \nofficial  position,  felt  obliged  to  keep  himself  in  the \nbackground,  but  his  brother,  Pierre  E.  Skjoldebrand, \nthenceforth  took  an  active  part  in  the  negotiations \nbetween  the  United  States  and  Algiers.  November \n13,  1793,  the  brothers  wrote  letters  of  sympathy  and \nadvice  to  Colonel  Humphre^^s.  One  piece  of  advice \nwas  to  break  relations  with  a  Jew  merchant  in  Algiers, \nnamed  Bassara,  who  had  been  employed  by  the  Amer- \nicans as  an  agent  and  who  was  out  of  favor  with  the \ndey,  and  transfer  the  business  to  Bacri,  another  Jew. \nThis  was  done  and  helped  to  facilitate  matters.  But \nthe  dey  was  indisposed  to  peace.  He  said :  \"  If  I  were \nto  make  peace  with  everybody,  what  should  I  do  with \nmy  corsairs?  What  should  I  do  with  my  soldiers? \n^  Narr.  and  Grit.  Hist,  vii,  p.  360 ;  Nav.  AS.  i,  pp.  6,  8.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1793
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
