        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Some years ago a tall tower stood at the extreme \nend of Cape Marabata; the Christians called tt Torre \nBlanquilla (White Tower) and it was known to the \nMohammedans as Fl-Minar. All day long the tower \nlooked out on the sea; at night it waa tiled to sleep by \nthe murmur of the wind on the water. It was an \nancient tower whose walls were covered with gnarled \nvines; scorptons hid between her stones, and evil jinn \ngathered nearby at nightfall. The gypsies, who knew \nabout all things, sat the tower was built by the \nPortuguese who came here to fight against the \nMohammedans. The mountaineers of Andjera are \nbetter informed; they say the tower was built by Lass \nel-Behar the pirate in order to hide bis treasures with- \nin tts walls.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
