      },
      {
        "finding_id": "section-1ccf618187892711a901",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "None of these “explanations” of the Renegadoes gets us \nany closer to their possible motives for embracing Islam \nalong with the life of the Barbary corsairs. Brilliant traitors \nor assimilated heroes —neither stereotype possesses any real \ndepth. Both contain elements of truth. The pirates did intro- \nduce certain technical and strategic novelties to Barbary, as \nwe shall see. And they did participate in Islam in more com- \nplex ways than simply as hired thugs —or “experts” —as we \nshall also see. But we still have no inkling of the “why?” of the \nwhole phenomenon. We should note at once that although \nsome of the Renegadoes were literate in numerous lan- \nguages, none were /iterati. We have no firsthand accounts, no \ntexts by Renegadoes. Their social origins did not dispose \nthem to self-analytical writing; that luxury was still a monop- \noly of the aristocracy and emerging middle class. The pen of \nhistory is in the hand of the enemies of the Renegadoes; they \nthemselves are silent.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
          "source_file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 15291,
          "end_char": 16291,
          "start_line": 492,
          "end_line": 508,
          "printed_page": null,
