      {
        "finding_id": "section-c80a4b556b013901b843",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "was extinguished only in the 19th century. \nFrom 1659 onwards the coast cities of Algeria \nand Tunisia, though nominally forming parts \nof the Turkish empire, were in fact anarchical \nmilitary republics which chose their own \nrulers and lived by plunder. The maritime side \nof this long-lived brigandage was conducted \nby captains, or reises, who formed a class or \neven a corporation. Cruisers were fitted out by \ncapitalists and commanded by the retses. The \ntreasury of the pasha or his successors who \nbore the title of Agha or Dey or Bey, received \n10% of the value of the prizes.... Until the 17th \ncentury the pirates used galleys, but Simon \nDanser, a Flemish renegade, taught them the \nadvantages of using sailing ships. In the first \nhalf of the 17th century more than 20,000 cap- \ntives were said to be imprisoned in Algiers \nalone. The rich were allowed to redeem them- \nselves, but the poor were condemned to slav- \nery. Their masters would not in many cases \nallow them to secure freedom by professing \nMohammadanism. Inthe early part of the 19th \ncentury, Tripolitania, owing to its piratical \npractices, was several times involved in war \nwith the United States. After the general paci- \nfication of 1815, the British made two vain \nattempts to suppress Algerian piracy, which \nwas ended only by the French conquest of \nAlgiers in 1830.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1659,
          1815,
          1830
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
