      {
        "finding_id": "section-20096130e8484773fc8e",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "ily of sea-rovers (probably Albanian in origin but resident on \nLesbos), who first arrived in the Western Mediterranean as \nan agent of the declining Mameluke power of Egypt. From \nTunis, he and his brothers joined with Moors from Granada \nto raid Spanish coasts. They raised their own freelance fleet \nand sold their services to various North African regimes; \nwhen possible they would assassinate the local ruler and take \nover the town (Bougie, 1512, Jijelli, 1514, Algiers, 1515); the \nisland of Djerba for a time served as their headquarters. \nAround 1518, hard pressed by Spain, Khaireddin appealed \nfor aid to the Ottoman Sultan Selim I (the “Grim”), and was \nappointed vice-regent or éeylerbey of Algiers. He finally man- \naged to expel the Spaniards from their island fortress in the \nbay of Algiers in 1529, and took Tunis in 1534.10 The emper- \nor appointed him admiral of the entire Turkish fleet. The \nOttomans had a treaty with France at the time, and \nBarbarossa appeared off the coast of Provence as an ally. But \nso powerful was he that he prohibited the ringing of church \nbells (an offensive sound in Islamic tradition) while his fleet \nwas anchored in port. He died in bed in his palace at \nConstantinople, and was succeeded as beylerbey of Algiers \nby his son Hassan Barbarossa. A true pirate epic, rags to \nriches: the Renegadoes’ dream. [Spencer, 1976: 18]",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1512,
          1514,
          1515,
          1518,
          1529,
          1534,
          1976
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
