      {
        "finding_id": "section-5d839e33833540208004",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Ali Bitchnin probably had ambitions to \nusurp control over the regency. His alliance \nwith the sultan of Koukou, his bodyguard of \nhundreds of soldiers, his personal navy, his \nrelations with the coulougli leaders all point to \npolitical ambitions. He suffered a serious \nreverse at Valona, where he lost eight galleys \n(Knight secured his freedom from him in that \nbattle; he was a slave on board of one of the \nships that was captured) and two thousand \nslaves. A few years later, when the sultan \nplanned an assault on Malta, Ali Bitchnin \nrefused to allow the Algerian naval forces to go \nunless the sultan would pay a subsidy in \nadvance. The Sublime Porte sent a chaouch \n(messenger or emissary) to Algiers to secure \nAli Bitchnin’s head; both the chaouch and the \npasha had to flee to a mosque to escape the \nwrath of the corsair admiral’s followers. At",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
          "source_file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
