        "evidence_excerpt": "French agreed on condition of the safe return \nof the Jesuits, which was done. In 1609 \nDanser was reunited with his family and \nrestored to full citizenship by the Marseilles \ncity council. But, once a corsair always a cor- \nsair, whether in the service of Christian France \nor Muslim Algiers, and in 1610 Danser pre- \nsented to the king and the Marseilles coun- \ncilors a bold proposal for an expedition against \nAlgiers which — given his extraordinary inside \nknowledge of the city—would probably have \noverthrown the Regency government. \nUnfortunately, the French, distrustful of the \nloyalty of the former corsair, refused to enter- \ntain his project.” [Spencer, pp. 125-6]",
