      {
        "finding_id": "section-b62252cbdc6bd35a84f5",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The ambiguity of the Renegadoes was mirrored even in \nlanguage. The medley of peoples in Algiers must have pro- \nduced a polyglot nightmare of mistranslation. A lingua fran- \nca was needed, and indeed came to be known as Franco, the \nlanguage of the “Franks” (and by extension of all European \nforeigners), or Sabir (from the Spanish “to know”). Arabic, \nSpanish, Turkish, Italian, and Provengal were mixed in this \ntypical seaport argot. If a parallel dialect developed in Salé, \nit might have utilized Arabic, Berber, Hispano-Arabic \n(Morisco) and Spanish, Portuguese, French, and English. \n“New” languages reflect new and unique large-scale social \nphenomena; they are not simply means of communication \nbut also patterns for thinking, vehicles for the inner and outer \nexperience of the speakers, for their new communitas, and \ntheir new (or newly-adopted) ideology. Franco died out with \nthe corsairs, but its shadowy existence suggests that the \nRenegadoes had become —however tenuously —a “People”, \na linguistic community. Given the right historical circum- \nstances, a lingua franca can become a full-fledged literary \nlanguage, like Urdu or Bahasa Malay. Franco never made the \ngrade—but knowing that it existed must change our view of \nthe Renegadoes. We can no longer see them as a random \nscattering of lost apostates. A language (however crude and \njury-rigged) is a culture, or at least the sure sign of an emerg- \ning culture.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
          "source_file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
