        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Probably the corsair about whom we know the most was \nJohn Ward. Ward enjoyed the distinction of “starring” as the \nvillain of that 1612 West End hit, A Christian Turn 0 Turke; \nWard also merited at least two penny-dreadful blackletter \npamphlets and two popular ballads—the supermarket",
