      {
        "finding_id": "section-02dfd81a60fef32b04fe",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Ward was born around 1553, “a poore fisher’s brat” in \nFaversham, Kent. In the last year of Elizabeth’s reign and the \nfirst of James, we find him penniless in Plymouth, apparent- \nly with a fairly extensive career in privateering behind him— \nfifty years old, “squat, bald, white-haired.” [Norris, 1990: 63] \nIn 1603 he had the extreme bad luck to be “drummed into \nservice” in the Navy—i.e., impressed —and forced to serve \naboard the Lions Whelp under Captain Thomas Sockwell \n(who later became a pirate himself). As many historians have \nnoted, low or non-existent pay, exhausting drudgery, and \nviolent corporal punishments made up life in the Navy in \nthose days, which was “one of the worst fates that could \nbefall any man.”!2 Ward is said to have lamented his salad \ndays in privateering “when we might sing, drab [i.e., fuck], \nswear and kill men as freely as your cakemakers do flies; \nwhen the whole sea was our empire where we robbed at will, \nand the world was our garden where we walked for sport.” \nAfter just two weeks of naval discipline Ward reasserted \nhimself and organized thirty other sailors to jump ship, steal \na small bark in Plymouth harbor,!3 and sail out on the \nAccount, free men at last. Aged 50, Ward embarked on a \nnew and amazing career —as a pirate.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1553,
          1603,
          1990
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
