      },
      {
        "finding_id": "section-a892e79dd1342192f5fa",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "14. Six years later, in 1609, Ward and his comrade Captain Bishop \nvisited Munster again at least once. Local officials had to be impris- \noned for dealing with the pirates, who, after all, had 10 or 11 ships \nand about 1,000 men. Unable to repel them by force the English \n“Vice-President” of Munster tried to pardon them instead — but this \nexpedient also failed. Later that year the British Lord Admiral sent \na ship to Barbary under one Captain Pepwell to persuade Ward and \nhis confederates “to forsake their wicked course of life.” His mission \nnot only failed, but all his sailors deserted him and joined Ward. \nPepwell had to “part with his pinnace at an under rate to the Turks” \nand return to London looking foolish. Captain Bishop, who now \nclaimed to despise Ward for turning Turke (in 1609), was bribed to \nmurder him, but failed. Bishop pleaded for a pardon, saying supine- \nly: “I will die a poor labourer in mine own country, if I may, rather \nthan be the richest pirate in the world.” [Ewen, 1939: 20-21] Ward \nobviously had other plans.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1609,
          1939
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
          "source_file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 81140,
          "end_char": 82194,
          "start_line": 2077,
          "end_line": 2092,
          "printed_page": null,
