        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "15. In or about 1604, Ward arrived in Salé “to victuall and tryme his \nshippe haveing sould all their goodes”; there he joined with other \npirates to raise and “disburse £100 to redeem a countryman” from \ncaptivity [Ewen, 1939: 3]. Ward used his own money to ransom \ncaptives on several other known occasions; perhaps this was his \nmethod of “giving to the poor”.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1604,
          1939
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
          "source_file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
