        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Yet this was just the start of a series of dis- \nasters that lay in store for Ward in the winter \nof 1607-8. First, the prize of which he had \ntaken command was lost at sea, and then a \ngalleon, which he had captured and fitted out \nat Navarino, was wrecked. Worse still, one of \nhis leading captains, a Fleming named Jan \nCasten, was off Modone on 21 March 1608 \nwith two men-of-war and a prize when he was \nsurprised and defeated by the Venetian gal- \nleys. In this, one of their rare victories over the \npirates, the Venetians killed 50 men, including \nCasten, and captured forty-four more.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1607,
          1608
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
