        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Lithgow also tells us that in his old age Ward had \nbecome interested in the problem of incubating poultry eggs \nin camel dung. One imagines him pottering about the \nalabaster palace with pots of this odiferous mulch, accompa- \nnied by curious chickens. The inevitable “bad end” which all \npirates must suffer was provided by the plague, which paid \none of its regular visits to North Africa in 1623. Aged about \nseventy, Ward died in bed and was buried at sea just as he’d \nalways expected and hoped.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1623
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
