        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "16. Once in 1608, Ward sailed into Algiers with a Spanish prize \nladen with a cargo of “alligant wines”, and there met another pirate \n(one John King of Limehouse) who'd just captured a ship carrying \nbeer. Ward traded him a tun of wine for a tun of beer, losing money \non the deal, and revealing his working-class taste! [Ewen, 1939: 9]",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1608,
          1939
