        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Around the same time one of Salé’s most important \nsaints —of the learned and orthodox variety —settled in the \ncity: Sidi Ahmad Ibn Ashir, “the doctor”, teacher of such \nfamous Sufis as Ibn Abbad of Ronda, and also of a more \nmaraboutic figure, a coral fisherman from Turkey known \nsimply as “the Turk”, who became a sort of patron-saint of \nlocal sailors. Sidi Ahmad Ibn Ashir himself could bless the \nocean and quiet storms, so that his tomb later became a pop- \nular pilgrimage for pirates.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
