        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The newly-arrived Moriscos however were even more \noutlandish—they spoke Hispano-Arabic or even Spanish, \nhad Christian names and no wealth at all, and seemed even \nmore vulgar than the Hornacheros. So the Moriscos had to \ncontent themselves with land below the Casbah (part of pre- \nsent-day Rabat), where they constituted a wholly separate \ngroup unto themselves. They thirsted for revenge against \nSpain and quickly became enthusiastic corsairs.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
