      {
        "finding_id": "section-3717711ae182aa878935",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "The Bou Regreg Republic may have lost some autono- \nmy under the régime of the Dala’iyya, but perhaps gained — \nat last—some peace and balance under the nominal valtanat \nof the Sufi order. In any case, the last two decades of the \nTriple Republic were its most golden, at least in terms of \npiracy. Freed at last of internecine strife, all three city-states \ncould turn all their hostility outward—in the corsair holy \nwar. Moreover, if the corsair republics in their purest form \n(1614-1640) were unique as political entities, one can only \nuse a pleonasm like “more unique” to describe the condo- \nminium-régime of corsairs and Sufis, which lasted from 1640 \nto 1660. It boggles the imagination —and indeed it was too \ngood to last long. The hand of the Dala’iyya and its chief in \nSalé—Sidi Abdullah the “prince of Salé” —came to feel heav- \nier and heavier to the Andalusians and pirates. They began \nto look for some means to restore their pristine state of total \nindependence, which by now had come to take on all the \naura of an ancient and revered tradition.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1614,
          1640,
          1660
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
          "source_file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
          "start_char": 134359,
          "end_char": 135427,
          "start_line": 3415,
          "end_line": 3432,
          "printed_page": null,
          "scan_indexes_0_based": [],
          "pdf_file": null,
