        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Captured at Lanzarote in 1618 by Barbary Corsairs, \nJanz apostasized at Algiers—and although the conversion \nmay have been forced, it seems to have taken root, for Murad \nnever begged a pardon or gave the least sign of wishing to \nreturn to Christendom. He took up his trade under the lead- \nership of the great Algerian corsair Sulayman Rais (who may \nalso have been Dutch) who died however next year in 1619. \nMurad provides us with a perfect example of the links \nbetween Algiers and Salé, since he now began to move back \nand forth between them like a man with dual citizenship.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1618,
          1619
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
