        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "By 1627 the political situation in Salé had grown a bit \nwarm. The Hornacheros declared their own Republic in the \nCasbah that year, and al-Ayyashi was actively establishing \nhimself in Old Salé. Murad’s Admiralship, which had kept \nhim from sea, may have ended awkwardly; in any case, after \nhis return from Iceland he moved with his Moorish family \nback to Algiers, and at once resumed the active Corsair life. \nIn 1631 he organized another great adventure, his sacking of \nthe town of Baltimore, County Cork, Ireland.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1627,
          1631
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
