        "evidence_excerpt": "The real and still unanswered question about the sack of \nBaltimore is not “how?” Although Murad’s seamanship was \nobvously superb, he was by no means a pioneer in this case, \nas with Iceland. “Little John” Ward had visited Ireland sev- \neral times and we can be sure he wasn’t the only corsair to \nfollow that route.29",
