      {
        "finding_id": "section-cf5cfadf67f25b5256a6",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Munster, summed up the state of the province \nin 1589 in these words: “If piracies be there \nmaintained, and every port and haven in those \nparts be made acceptable for them, we must \ngive over our inhabitation there, since we shall \npass neither our commodities or ourselves over \nthe seas, but at their mercy. The province gen- \nerally is made a receptacle of pirates. They are \ntoo much favoured in Kerry. Sir Edward \nDenny has received Gascon wine which was \nrobbed from Frenchmen, and Lany Denny has \nreceived goods which were taken from \n‘Brittaines.’ One Captain Maris, of Youghal, a \nknown negotiator in these kinds of affairs, is \nshortly to remove to Tawlaght, a castle of Sir \nEdward Denny’s, near Tralee, there to exer- \ncise that trade.” Denny, later created Earl of \nNorwich, also had seats in Cornwall, and was \ntherefore a neighbour to the Killigrews. He, in \nfact, did for the pirates in Ireland what the \nKilligrews and Sir John Perrot did for them in \nCornwall and South Wales. When influential \nnoblemen acted as “fences” piracy was certain- \nly a paying game... As the Royal Navy was \npractically non-existent until the latter half of \nthe century, when James II placed it on a \nsound basis, it was virtually impossible “to eye \nand awe the inhabitants from traffic with these",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1589
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
          "source_file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
