        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "pirates would send a party of men ashore to \nfetch them after dark. These would fire off a \nmusket or two as though they were making a \nland raid. The local people, amply forwarned, \nwould keep well out of the way. The business \nwas very welcome, said Mainwaring, because \ncattle sold by this means usually fetched dou- \nble their market value.",
