      {
        "finding_id": "section-4de10daa8575c2cdb561",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Hackett might have had a “deeper” reason for his odd behav- \nior. All that we know about him derives from his own testi- \nmony at his trial, when presumably he was trying to justify \nhis actions with some cover story. What if the “scooping up” \nof Hackett’s vessel off Kinsale was not an accident but a ren- \ndevous? What if Hackett, a Catholic, were an agent of the \nCatholic Sir Walter Coppinger? What if Coppinger had been \nin touch with corsair representatives—easy enough in \nCounty Cork, it would seem —and had suggested a raid on \nBaltimore? Perhaps he painted it as a richer prize than it \nproved in fact, or perhaps he sweetened the suggestion with \nan offer of payment —he could afford it. And maybe on June \n19 Hackett deliberately put his boat in the way of “capture”, \nso he could act as pilot and guide to the corsairs. (We know \nthe corsairs a/ways sought out such experts, like the Moriscos \nwho acted as spies in Spain, or the Danish slave who guided \nMurad to Iceland.) A lot of pure conjecture, of course. \nBut...keep an eye on Hackett.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
          "source_file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
