        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Salé-Rabat, of course, was beholden to no outside gov- \nernment in the first half of the 17th century, but commis- \nsioned corsairs in the name of the Republic; and the Republic \nconsisted—more-or-less—of the corsairs themselves. \nAlgiers, Tunis, and Tripoli have been called “corsair states”, \nbut in truth only “Sallee” deserves that definition.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
