      {
        "finding_id": "section-fa3643cfe786a9f277a4",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Clearly Rabat/Salé was not organized like a pure pirate \nventure — but it was not organized like a European or Islamic \nmonarchy either. The big difference between Algiers and Salé \nwas that the “tax” off the top went to Istanbul in the first case, \nbut in the second case, stayed tn Salé. It was used to benefit the \ncorsairs (repair the ramparts, finance expeditions, etc.) rather \nthan to fatten some distant sultan. Salé’s wars with the \nSaadians, the Marabout al-Ayyashi, and the Alewite dynasty, \netc., all centered around the 10%, which was both the symbol \nand the cost of corsair independence. Salé was neither as \nanarchic nor as communistic as “Libertatia” (see below) or \nother real-life pirate utopias—but it was far more so than any \nEuropean country. Its Governor-Admiral and its Divan were \nelected and could be un-elected every year if they failed to \nrepresent the people's interests. Everyone capable of shipping \non a cruise stood a chance at wealth. Even “captives of war” \ncould earn freedom and wealth as Renegadoes. As for the \nprofessional pirates who joined the Republic, once again we \nsee that although they lost the pure autonomy of real piracy, \nthey gained a home, a society, a source of backing, a market, \nand a place to enjoy their wealth—everything a pirate might \nwell lack and most yearn for. It was worth taking a cut in pay \nto gain all that, obviously.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
          "source_file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
