        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "In the 17th century Winter was still an off-season for \nmerchant shipping, corsairs, and even grand navies. The cor- \nsairs followed a seasonal pattern and spent at least three or \nfour months every year at home in Salé, attending to politics \nor love affairs, married life or debauch, wheeling and deal- \ning, repairing and shipbuilding—or perhaps even to the \npractise of Sufism —according to their wonts and wants.",
