        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Most European visitors hated Salé: “an habitation for vil- \nlaines, a den for theeves, a receptacle for pirats, a rendezvouze \nfor renegodoes, a slaughter-house of barbarous cruelty and \nsavage barbarisme, a bane and confusion to shipping-mer- \nchants and merchandise, and a miserable dolefull dungeon for \npoore captived Christians” [Sources (nédites, 1935: 376.] But for \nvarious odd reasons, some Europeans actually liked Salé.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1935
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
