      {
        "finding_id": "section-6a89cbf5ccc1bbf551c2",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "But the feare is some maie abuse their comis- \nsions and turne pirattes, and Englishmen goe out to \nsea in their shippes, the shippes of Sallye, and serve \nunder them and turne renegadors; so His Majestie \nlooseth subjectes and God so many soules, which \nallso I submitt to further consideracion to be \nrestreyned by some severe proclamacion, yea, \nrather to be wished (thoughe I have ben ymploied \nand in that respect maie seme a frinde to Sallye, yet, \n“magis amica patria” the honour of my countrey and \ngenerall good of Christendome is neerer and deerer \nto me), I saie, thoughe I have ben a meanes of that \ntreutie of peace thereby to redeme Your Majesties \nsubjectes oute of captivitie (as I have ben this time \nallso for the Frenche), yet nowe that, both the one \nand the other, all the English and French captives \nare cleared from thence, I could wishe, I saie, Your \nMajestie and brother of Fraunce wolde joyne yor \nforces for the suppressing of all the shippes belong- \ning to that place, and Argier likewise, to prevent \nboth theis and other inconveniences or rather indig- \nnities, Lastima! a pitifull case, so many Christians \ndaylie taken by their shippes and made slaves, yea, \na greate nomber forced to forsake their faithe, turne \nTurkes and renegadors, which maie easelie be reme- \ndied, if it please Your Majestie to take into consid- \neracion the motives hereunto annexed. [s6i0., p. 114]",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
