        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "rogues dressed half-Turk half-European, which would sug- \ngest a setting in Algiers or Tunis; but we can extrapolate to \nMorocco. No wine bottles are in sight, yet the corsairs are \nfloating along in a hilarious mood. One, in a dervish hat dec- \norated with jasmine or some other flower, is about to eat \nsomething that looks like a sweetmeat. What else could it be \nbut mayoun, the famous North African concoction of hashish, \nnuts, fruit, honey, butter, etc, which Baudelaire and his com- \nrades imitated so poorly with their mint-jelly confitures?",
        "years_in_scope": [],
