      {
        "finding_id": "section-cc88e3a70d6aa42a6089",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Burg’s Sodomy and the Pirate Tradition (1984) makes the \nvery logical point that the generally all-male society of the \npirates, freed of all law and conventional morality, must have \nseemed an obvious world of refuge for the persecuted homo- \nsexuals of 17—18th century Europe —especially for mariners, \nwho were already known for such proclivities. Burg main- \ntains that the normal homosexual pirate affair would involve \nadult men—i.e., “androphile” homosexuality. Unfortunately \nfor this thesis Burg fails to document very many such rela- \ntions, and has to take most of his actual examples from the \nranks of boy-lovers instead. Here anecdotal and even \narchival evidence is plentiful. Burg however then goes on to \nstigmatize adult-youth relations as “pedophilia”, a current \nterm of clinical disapproval, tantamount to “child abuse”. \nBurg, who implies that his sociological judgements are based \non the ideology of “gay liberation” (which excludes boy-love \nfrom its roster of PC-ness), goes so far as to apply modern \ntherapeutical categories to pirate pederasts, whom he accus- \nes of “low self-esteem”, “feelings of inferiority, immaturity, \nand passivity”; they suffered from “deep-seated feelings of \ninferiority or hostility toward their social superiors,” etc., etc. \nAccording to Burg, the true pirate ideal was a “satisfying \nrelationship between men.”",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1984
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
