      {
        "finding_id": "section-5dd062d9e0d65de16c8e",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "And so, having followed our Corsairs’ calendar through \nthe social season—Winter—we return to Spring and the \nurge to set out once again roaming the open seas. I can’t say \nthat these scattered images of Renegado culture add up to any- \nthing like a hypothesis or a theory or even a very coherent \npicture. We've certainly had to use our imagination more \nthan a “real” historian would allow, erecting a lot of supposi- \ntions on a shaky framework of generalizations, and adding a \ntouch of fantasy (and what piratologist has ever been able to \nresist fantasy?). I can only say that I’ve satisfied my own \ncuriosity at least to this extent: That something like a \nRenegado culture could have existed; that all the ingredients for \nit were present, and contiguous, and synchronic. Moreover, \nthere exists good circumstantial evidence for this culture in \nwhat we might call its one great artifact—the Moorish \nCorsair Republic(s) of the Bou Regreg. Such an original \nconcept would almost seem to depend on a depth of origin \nwhich can only be labelled “cultural”, i.e., sociologically com- \nplex, and self-involved enough to be called (and to call itself) \ndifferent. The Mafia names itself “Our Thing”; the corsairs \ncalled their “thing” the Republic of Salé—not just a pirate \nhang-out or safe harbor, but a pirate utopia, a planned struc-",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
