      {
        "finding_id": "section-f3a9fa33d415af6993f3",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "tavern where they could squander their booty. They were \nprepared to accept temporary leadership in a combat situa- \ntion, but on shore they preferred absolute freedom even at \nthe price of violence. In pursuit of booty, they were willing to \nlive or die by radical democracy as an organizing principle; \nbut in the enjoyment of booty, they insisted on anarchy. \nSome shore-enclaves consisted of nothing more than a hid- \nden harbor, a beach where ships’ hulls could be scraped, and \na spring of clean water. Others were vicious little ports like \nPort Royal or Baltimore, run by “respectable” crooks like \nThomas Crooke, who were simply parasites on piracy. But \nother enclaves can really only be called intentional commu- \nnities —after all, they were intended, and they were commu- \nnal—and therefore can rightfully be considered as Pérate \nUtopias.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
