      {
        "finding_id": "section-6a57c4bb12fcbc7ebc6f",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "In the early 1700's the scene of action shifted from the \nCaribbean to the Indian Ocean. Europe had begun its colo- \nnialist-imperialist relations with the “Near” East and India, \nbut a great deal of territory remained “untamed”. The perfect \nlocation for land-enclaves proved to be Madagascar, conve- \nniently located near the Islamic pilgrimage sea route to \nArabia and Mecca. The famous Capt. Avery established a leg- \nend by scoring the imperial Moghul dhow on its way from \nIndia to the Hajj, winning a diamond the size of an egg, and \n“marrying” a Moghul princess; the diamond and other jewels \nwere reputedly buried somewhere around or in Boston \nHarbor and have never been recovered. Other pirates had no \ndesire to return to either America or Europe, and \nMadagascar looked promising. Neither Islam nor \nChristianity had penetrated the huge island, which remained \ntribal, pagan, and even “megalithic” in its hundreds of Native \n“kingdoms”. [For Megalithic practices in Madagascar, see \nMohen, 1990: 55-58] Some tribes proved eager for alliances",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1700,
          1990
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
          "source_file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
