      {
        "finding_id": "section-29118f585fe19722657f",
        "file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Pirate Utopias: Moorish Corsairs & European Renegadoes",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Hakim Bey"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1995-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "We must admit that the Tew problem casts the Mission \nnarrative in a somewhat apocryphal light; however, I believe \nthat the verdict of nonexistence is forced and over-hasty. \nSeveral other logical possibilities should be considered: (a) \nMission existed and the Manuscript existed, but contained \nmisinformation about Capt. Tew (perhaps the name Tew was \nused to mask someone else), which Defoe uncritically \naccepted; (b) the Manuscript existed and described real \nevents, but Defoe himself invented the episodes concerning \nTew (including the “anarchist” schism) for reasons of his \nown, perhaps to flesh out a sparse narrative; (c) the \nManuscript never existed, nor did any persons named \nMission or Caraccioli—but some experiment like Libertatia \nactually occured in Madagascar, and was thinly fictionalized \nby Defoe (Robinson Crusoe had a real-life model in \nAlexander Selkirk, a genuine castaway survivor). “Johnson” \nadded the name of a real pirate, Tew, to pump up the \nverisimilitude of the text, failing to realize that he was there- \nby giving the game away to future historians. None of these \nhypotheses can be proven or disproven on the basis of the \nTew problem. Therefore the Revisionist Debunking \nHypothesis—complete fictionalization—must also remain \nunproven. The mere passion for debunking should not be",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
          "url": "https://archive.org/details/pirate-utopias-hakim-bey",
          "source_file": "pirate-utopias-hakim-bey_Pirate_Utopias_Bey_0_djvu.txt",
