        "source_text_sha256": "ebef0a63c86f8eca812a0716c8fde4bac770ce246530d69bc074d6640e161000",
        "evidence_excerpt": "However, the comparison cannot be stretched too far. \nSalé was undoubtedly more libertarian than the Barbary \nCoast states of Algiers, Tunis, and Tripoli, but it certainly \nhad far more conventional structure than any of the pure \nPirate Utopias. The pirates of Salé clearly decided to accept \na republican form of government (and the 10% tax) in order \nto safeguard their liberties on a (hopefully) permanent basis; \nSalé can be seen as a sort of compromise.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
