      {
        "finding_id": "section-ca8803b5cce63837a085",
        "file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "•  Of  the  corsairs  dealt  with  in  this  record  of  their \n{  deeds  the  two  Barbarossas  were  the  sons  of  a  Mo- \nj  hammedan  father  and  a  Christian  mother.  Dragut \nReis  was  a  pure  Mohammedan,  and  AH  Basha  was \na  pure-blooded  Italian.  All  these  men,  as  will  be \nseen,  raised  themselves  to  eminence  in  the  pro- \nfession of  piracy ;  in  each  and  every  separate  case \nstarting  at  the  very  bottom  rung  of  the  ladder  and \nrising,  by  sheer  stress  of  valour  and  character,  to \nthe  very  top.  Each  in  turn  became  Admiralissimo \nto  the  Grand  Turk  at  Constantinople.  Kheyr-ed- \nDin  Barbarossa  commanded  the  Ottoman  fleet  at \nthe  great  battle  of  Prevesa,  at  which  he  met  with \nhis  life-long  competitor  at  sea,  the  famous  Genoese \nAdmiral,  Andrea  Doria.  Dragut  Reis  was  killed \nat  the  siege  of  Malta  in  1565,  and  Ali  Basha  was \nthe  only  Moslem  commander  who  increased  his \nreputation  at  the  battle  of  Lepanto  in  1571,  when \nDon  John  of  Austria  shattered  the  power  of  the \nMoslem  at  sea  for  the  time  being.",
        "years_in_scope": [
          1565,
          1571
        ],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
