        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "take  the  description  of  his  position  from  the  pages \nof  the  good  Padre  Alberto  Guglielmotti.  The \nFranciscan  says :  \"He  [that  is,  Abd-  Allah]  desired \npeace  with  all  and  prosperity  for  his  own  interests. \nFriendly  to  the  merchants  in  their  commerce ; \nfriendly  to  the  corsairs  in  their  spoils.  Let  all \nhold  by  the  law :  the  former  contentedly  paying \ncustoms  dues,  th^  latter  cheerfully  handing  over \na  fifth  part  of  their  robberies,  and  Abd-Allah — \ntheir  common  friend  —  would  ever  continue  at \npeace  with  them  all.  Outside  his  ports  the  mer- \nchants and  the  pirates  might  fall  by  the  ears  if \nthey  would  :  that  was  no  reason  for  him  to  trouble \nhis  head.  On  the  contrary,  he  would  joyfully  await \nthem  on  their  return  either  with  customs  dues  or \ntribute  of  the  fifth  as  the  case  might  be.\"",
