        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "from  the  struggling  corsairs  on  the  littoral  of  Northern \nAfrica,  and  was  a  sovereign  of  such  great  and \nmysterious  might  that  any  man  with  a  less  fine \ninstinct  into  the  psychology  of  the  times  in  which \nhe  lived  than  Kheyr-ed-Din  would  have  hesitated \nlong  and  anxiously  before  addressing  him  directly ; \nwould  probably  in  the  end  not  have  done  so  at  all. \nBut  desperate  diseases  require  desperate  remedies, \nand  the  politic  corsair  well  knew  that  even  the  moral \nsupport  of  such  an  one  as  the  Sultan  of  Constanti- \nnople was  worth  more  than  even  material  aid  from  a \nSultan  of  Tunis.",
