        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "His  next  act  was  to  defeat  the  corsair,  Cadolin, \nwho  had  eight  galleys  to  Doria's  six ;  these  he \nadded  to  his  own  fleet,  which  now  consisted  of \nfourteen  vessels,  he  having  begun  with  three.  As \nCadolin  was  one  of  the  most  famous  corsairs  of  the \nday,  this  capture  made  an  immense  sensation,  and \nall  men,  Moslems  as  well  as  Christians,  were  asking \none  another,  \"  Who  was  this  Doria  ?  \"",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
