      {
        "finding_id": "section-6c9bd7f0bf3e640e3dff",
        "file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Kheyr-ed-Din,  now  firmly  established  in  Algiers, \ndevoted  his  energies  to  the  undoing  of  his  Christian \nfoes  by  the  systematic  plunder  of  their  merchant- \nvessels.  At  this  period  he,  personally,  seems  to \nhave  remained  ashore,  and  sent  his  young  and \naspiring  captains  to  sea  to  increase  his  wealth  by \nplunder,  his  consequence  by  the  hordes  of  slaves \nwhich  they  swept  into  the  awful  bagnios  of  Algiers  ; \nand  Sandoval,  that  quaint  and  delightful  historian, \nis  moved  to  indignation  and  complains  with  much \nacrimony  of  \"las  malas  obras  que  este  corsario \nhizo  a  la  Chris tiandad \"  (the  evil  deeds  done  to \nChristianity  by  this  corsair).  These  were  on  so \nconsiderable  a  scale  at  this  time  that  he  had  to \ndevote  to  them  far  more  space  than  he  considered \nconsonant  with  the  dignity  of  history.",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
