        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Sailing  through  the  Straits  of  Bonifacio,  they \ntouched  Monte  Cristo,  a  small  island  where  they \nfound  a  slave  who  had  formerly  belonged  to  Deli- \nzuff. This  man  was  base  enough  to  betray  his  own \nnative  island  of  Biba  into  the  hands  of  the  corsairs, \nwho  sacked  it  thoroughly  and  carried  off  its  inhabi- \ntants ;  they  also  captured  thirteen  large  ships  going \nto  Sicily  for  wheat,  and  burnt  them,  making  slaves \nof  their  crews.  In  the  fight  with  these  vessels  Deli- \nzuff was  killed.  Shortly  after  this,  some  disagree- \nment arising  between  the  crews  of  the  ships  of \nBarbarossa  and  the  men  in  Delizuff's  fleet,  the \nAlgerian  commander  seized  a  man  out  of  one  of \nDelizufFs  galleys  and  had  him  summarily  shot. \nThe  death  of  Delizuff  naturally  caused  some  con- \nfusion in  his  command,  and  the  high-handed  pro- \nceeding of  Kheyr-ed-Din  caused  great  resentment, \nnot  unmixed  with  fear,  as  the  terror  inspired  by  the \nBarbarossas  was  a  very  real  sentiment.  Under  their",
