      {
        "finding_id": "section-e7ab0a2bfb545aef092e",
        "file": "seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_seawolvesofmedit00curruoft_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "It  is  somewhat  difficult  to  fathom  the  reasons \nwhich  induced  Barbarossa  to  treat  Soliman  to  his \nsanctimonious  diatribe  concerning  the  King  of \nTunis  ;  coming,  as  it  did,  from  a  pirate,  it  was  merely \nludicrous,  and  could  not  for  one  instant  have  de- \nceived the  remarkably  shrewd  person  to  whom  it \nwas  addressed.  The  corsair  stated  the  facts  cor- \nrectly, but  the  reasons  which  led  to  an  Eastern  auto- \ncrat disposing  of  his  family  in  this  manner  were  so \nobvious  at  the  time  that,  if  Soliman  felt  any  emotion \nat  all  concerning  the  event,  it  was  probably  one  of \nadmiration  !  Regarded  from  the  practical,  apart \nfrom  the  sentimental  side,  what  the  proposition \namounted  to  was  that  Barbarossa  should  attack  a \nking  with  whom  the  Grand  Turk  had  no  sort  of \nquarrel,  and  that,  once  his  territory  had  been  reft \nfrom  him,  that  it  should  be  handed  over  to  the  ruler \nof  Constantinople  for  the  greater  glory  of  the  Sub- \nlime Porte.  What  mental  reservations  there  were  on \nthe  part  of  the  corsair  we  are  not  told,  but  had  Soliman \nknown  him  better  he  would  have  been  aware  that \nnever  had  Barbarossa  pulled  any  chestnuts  from  the \nfire  of  life  which  were  not  intended  for  his  own  eating,",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "UNRESOLVED",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
        "locator": {
