        "title": "Sea-wolves of the Mediterranean : the grand period of the Moslem corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/seawolvesofmedit00curruoft",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": "Currey, Edward Hamilton",
          "date": [
            "1913-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": null,
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "8ded5d2596f6b8b5da24b9515a2ae1cca80e39c88e17cfd932f28761d003774e",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Promptly,  hurriedly,  but  efficiently,  the  corsair \norganised  his  new  possession  :  such  laws  as  he \ndecreed  did  not  err  on  the  side  of  tenderness  towards \na  people  so  ungrateful  as  to  have  refused  his  pro- \ntection in  the  first  instance,  and  who  had  only \naccepted  the  gift  at  the  point  of  the  sword.  His \nnephew  Aisa,  a  man  young  in  years  but  a  past-gradu- \nate in  the  school  of  his  terrible  uncle,  was  left  in \ncharge,  while  Dragut  himself  sailed  once  more  with \nhis  fleet,  for,  as  it  is  put  by  the  Spanish  historian \nMarmol,  \"  truly  the  sea  was  his  element.\"",
        "years_in_scope": [],
