        "evidence_excerpt": "the  waggons  in  motion,  and  his  friend \nSekeletu  received  him  in  royal  style,  while \nthe  court  herald  leaped  and  shouted  adul- \natory sentences.  Livingstone's  presents  of  a \ncouple  of  cats  and  some  improved  goats  and \nfowls,  and  his  attempts  to  bring  in  a  superior \nbull,  which,  unfortunately,  had  to  be  left \nbehind,  gave  great  satisfaction.  His  approach \ncaused  a  precipitate  retreat  of  the  slave- \ntraders  and  Sekeletu  dealt  a  severe  blow  to \ntheir  aspirations  by  the  political  execution  of \nhis  rival  Inpepe.",
