        "source_text_sha256": "8d4d50eaf2b2a7a567e45f1745c54f1d7ef268dcc3cd5193895f31965f42ef69",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Day  by  day  Livingstone  became  more  de- \nbilitated. In  his  weak  state  the  din,  inseparable \nfrom  natives,  grew  very  trying.  An \nimpudent  laugh  by  one  of  his  own \npeople  to  a  request  for  silence  roused  him  to \nsuch  righteous  indignation  that  he  charged \nout  of  his  tent  with  his  double-barrelled  pistol \nand  created  a  stampede  and  fright  that  had \nthe  best  result.  Waking  from  a  state  of  coma \nthe  next  night,  he  found  that  his  men  had \nbuilt  a  stockade,  outside  of  which  a  party \nof  Chiboque  were  making  their  usual  de- \nmands. Parleying  and  extortion  were  brought \nto  an  end  at  the  expiration  of  three  days  by",
