      "title": "Our Navy and the Barbary Corsairs",
      "url": "https://archive.org/details/ournavyandbarba00allegoog",
      "identifier": null,
      "repository": null,
      "acquired_text_excerpt": "The first of the great corsairs were the brothers \nHoruk and Khair-ed-Din Barbarossa, natives of Lesbos, \nwho had in youth joined a gang of pirates in the east \nMediterranean. Not finding free scope for his ambi- \ntion so near the sultan's fieet, Horuk determined to \ntry his fortune on the Barbary coast. He first went to \nTunis in 1504, which he made his base. From Tunis \nand later from other ports he cruised with brilliant \nthough not uninterrupted success, making many cap- \ntures and collecting a strong fleet.^",
